<p><strong>A spa booking app lets guests choose a service, branch, therapist and time on their phone and receive a confirmation straight away. For spas in Nepal it captures bookings from residents and tourists around the clock, and stops double-bookings by locking the therapist, the room and the time together. Zennly provides this for one spa or many.</strong></p>
<p>Visitors to Thamel, Lakeside in Pokhara, Sauraha near Chitwan and the Kathmandu Valley decide on a massage or spa day on their phone, often the same day and often late in the evening. A spa that only takes bookings by phone or by message misses many of them. A spa that shows live availability and confirms instantly does not.</p>
<h2>What guests expect from a spa booking app</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Live availability</strong> &ndash; choose the service, branch and time, with no waiting for a reply.</li>
<li><strong>Instant confirmation</strong> &ndash; a booking number straight away, so there is something to show at the door.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile first</strong> &ndash; most visitors book from a phone. See <a href="/features/booking/">online booking</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What your team needs behind the page</h2>
<p>A booking page is only half the system. Behind it the spa needs the therapist and the room booked together, a payment record by cash, card or online, and manager approval for discounts. Without these, online booking just moves the chaos from the phone to the screen. Read <a href="/blog/how-to-manage-a-spa-in-nepal/">how to manage a spa in Nepal</a>.</p>
<h2>Peak and quiet seasons</h2>
<p>Tourist-area spas have busy autumn and spring weeks and quieter months. Online booking with staff and room scheduling keeps busy weeks organised, while daily and monthly <a href="/features/reports/">reports</a> show which services and therapists carry the quiet months. Use <a href="/features/campaigns/">campaigns</a> to run a dated offer that shows on the booking page.</p>
<h2>Memberships, packages and vouchers</h2>
<p>Many spas sell prepaid cards, session bundles and gift vouchers. Zennly tracks <a href="/features/memberships/">memberships</a>, <a href="/features/packages/">packages</a> and <a href="/features/vouchers/">vouchers</a> with balances and expiry. See <a href="/blog/spa-memberships-packages-vouchers-nepal/">how to track them properly</a>.</p>
<h2>Try it for your spa</h2>
<p>See the booking flow for <a href="/solutions/spa/">spas and wellness centres</a>, or look at the cities we cover: <a href="/nepal/kathmandu/">Kathmandu</a> and <a href="/nepal/pokhara/">Pokhara</a>.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>Is there a spa booking app for Nepal?</h3>
      <p>Zennly gives spas in Nepal an online booking page that guests use from their phone, with staff, room and time booked together and every payment recorded.</p>
      <h3>Can tourists book a spa in Pokhara or Kathmandu online?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Visitors can pick a service, a time and a branch at any hour, which captures bookings made before they arrive or after the front desk closes.</p>
      <h3>Does an online spa booking system stop double-bookings?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Zennly locks the therapist, the room and the time together, so a slot that is taken cannot be booked again.</p>
      <h3>Can I manage several spa branches in one booking system?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Zennly runs one branch or many from one account with one daily report.</p>
      
